[
 {
  "kind": 1,
  "language": "markdown",
  "value": "# Lab 3: Real Weather from a Web API\n\n**Goal:** Connect your Broker to the live [Open-Meteo](https://open-meteo.com) weather API so your station fetches real outdoor conditions for your coordinates.\n\n**What you will build:**\n1. **`CampusWeather` (Connector):** Whenever any message is published to `campus/weather/request`, it makes an HTTP `GET` request to Open-Meteo and publishes the JSON response to `campus/weather/raw`. From there, `ProcessWeather` (from Lab 2) automatically converts it!\n2. **`RequestWeather` (Action):** Publishes `\"poll\"` to `campus/weather/request` every 5 minutes.\n\n> **Note:** A **Connector** (`DEFINE CONNECTOR`) bridges the Broker to an external system. Community Edition allows up to **3 Connectors** — this hackathon uses all 3 (1 here, and 2 in Lab 4)."
 },
 {
  "kind": 1,
  "language": "markdown",
  "value": "## 1. The `CampusWeather` Connector\n\nThe Broker automatically substitutes `{env.WEATHER_LAT}` and `{env.WEATHER_LON}` in the `ENDPOINT` URL using the environment variables you set in `00-setup`.\n\nTo update a Connector later, just edit the cell and click **▷ (Run Cell)** again — the new definition replaces the old one. (`DEFINE ROUTE` is the older spelling of `DEFINE CONNECTOR`; both work.)"
 },
 {
  "kind": 2,
  "language": "lot",
  "value": "DEFINE CONNECTOR CampusWeather WITH TYPE REST_API\n    ADD REST_API_CONFIG\n        WITH BASE_ADDRESS \"https://api.open-meteo.com\"\n        WITH ENABLE_CLIENT \"true\"\n        WITH USE_SSL \"true\"\n    ADD EVENT GetCurrentWeather\n        WITH SOURCE_TOPIC \"campus/weather/request\"\n        WITH DESTINATION_TOPIC \"campus/weather/raw\"\n        WITH METHOD \"GET\"\n        WITH ENDPOINT \"/v1/forecast?latitude={env.WEATHER_LAT}&longitude={env.WEATHER_LON}&current=temperature_2m,wind_speed_10m&wind_speed_unit=kmh\""
 },
 {
  "kind": 1,
  "language": "markdown",
  "value": "## 2. The `RequestWeather` Action\n\nThis timer Action triggers a weather poll every 5 minutes. The payload (`\"poll\"`) doesn't matter — `CampusWeather` triggers on any message arriving on `campus/weather/request` and reads the coordinates from your environment variables."
 },
 {
  "kind": 2,
  "language": "lot",
  "value": "DEFINE ACTION RequestWeather\nON EVERY 5 MINUTES DO\n    PUBLISH TOPIC \"campus/weather/request\" WITH \"poll\""
 },
 {
  "kind": 1,
  "language": "markdown",
  "value": "## Check It Worked\n\n**Don't wait 5 minutes for the timer!** Trigger a poll right now: open **Data Viewer → Publish** and publish `poll` to `campus/weather/request`.\n\nWithin a couple of seconds:\n1. The raw Open-Meteo response appears on `campus/weather/raw`.\n2. Your converted `WeatherReading` appears on `campus/weather/reading`.\n\n**Seeing a message on `campus/weather/errors` instead?** Inspect its payload. If it says *\"The service is overloaded\"*, Open-Meteo is temporarily rate-limiting requests — wait a minute and publish `poll` again.\n\nDocs: [REST API connectors](https://docs.coreflux.org/latest/lot-language/routes/rest-api-routes)."
 }
]
